<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor An of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">382–419</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Sima Dezong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor An of Jin, Sima Dezong, reigned over the Eastern Jin dynasty from 396 to 419 but was severely disabled and never ruled himself. In 403 the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huan-xuan">Huan Xuan</a> forced him to abdicate and proclaimed his own state of Chu. Liu Yu restored him in 404, and later had him killed in 419, shortly before founding the Liu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-an-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor An of Jin" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see below · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_drs_49802792_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E4%B8%89%E5%9C%8B%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E7%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8_v.1_(%E6%99%89%E5%AE%89%E5%B8%9D).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
